From 289edf5b0f99bc54b986bf1687b085d439616cd3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 09:17:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(gateway): always hand an externally-supervised gateway
 back before service restart [daveey]

Spec: a gateway process that declares an external supervisor restarts through the
graceful SIGUSR1 handback (restart_externally_supervised_gateway) before ANY
installed-service dispatch, the canonical service owner included.

d295a76236e narrowed that to services that do not own the gateway
(installed_service_owns_gateway: launchd/systemd job pid == gateway or its launcher
ancestor). That helper is removed; the pre-dispatch handback is unconditional, and the
canonical-owner test now asserts the handback (exit 75 drain, relaunch, no service call)
instead of the service path. RED/GREEN for that test: owner-red.log / owner-green.log.

The late external-supervisor check before the manual fallback is removed: every path that
reaches it already passed the identical pre-dispatch check, so it was dead code. The
manual fallback keeps refuse_restart_of_service_managed_gateway on a fresh pid read.

Test fixture: _FakeSupervisor.close() killed the first lookalike gateway, which woke the
relaunch watcher and could spawn a second child after teardown (a leaked
`gateway run --external-supervisor` lookalike). close() now sets a closed flag under the
relaunch lock first, joins the watcher, and reaps both children.
test_fake_supervisor_close_never_relaunches_after_teardown was RED on the old fixture
(second child spawned after close) and is GREEN now.

Tests: tests/hermes_cli/test_gateway_restart_installed_service_external_supervisor.py +
test_gateway_restart_external_supervisor.py 13 passed; the 131-file gateway/update
affected set 1606 passed, 0 failed, 48 skipped (hermes-core-wt test).

Behavior change to note: the canonical launchd plist runs `gateway run
--external-supervisor` and a systemd unit gateway answers identify with supervisor
"systemd", so canonical service restarts now also take the handback instead of
launchd_restart / systemd_restart (no plist/unit refresh, no wedged-loop SIGKILL
escalation, no kickstart fallback when the supervisor does not relaunch: exit 1).
